- **`ui` is the view, and `presentation` what the screens hold and decide (the Presentation Model).** Both come with
  `ui = "atomic"` in `.config/rotproof.toml`, and go together: a project with no screens declares `ui = "none"` and
  has neither, rather than listing them in `absent`. `ui` follows
  atomic design (`pages` > `templates` > `organisms` > `molecules` > `atoms`), `presentation` holds `models` and
  `display`, and each holds only its levels. Besides direction, the table limits what each level knows: only `pages`
  know the models, giving them the use cases `composition` passes in; `organisms` and `templates` know only the plain
  values of `presentation.display` and take actions as callbacks; `atoms` and `molecules` know nothing of
  `presentation` and take plain values; `ui` knows neither `application`, `domain` nor `infrastructure`. A model calls
  the input ports of `protocol.inbound` and draws nothing: a provider that hands its state to the view is a part of
  `ui`. What the whole UI shares goes in the lowest level that may know what it knows: a part that renders nothing (a
  design value, a hook, a provider of a theme) is an atom when it knows no project concept, and code beside the levels
  fails `rotproof check`.
